---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactBlock from '../../components/ContactBlock.astro';
import { COMPANY } from '../../lib/company';

/**
 * Every statement below is a property of the site as built, checkable in dist/:
 * this site's own code sets no cookie, no analytics script runs, and the only
 * third-party host any page requests is challenges.cloudflare.com — the Turnstile
 * widget on the enquiry forms, which this page now discloses. tests/legal.test.ts
 * asserts each of those, and the "no IP address" promise below is enforced against
 * the endpoint itself by tests/submit.test.ts, which is what makes it safe to state.
 * The 180-day figure is RETENTION_SECONDS in functions/api/submit.ts; the two must
 * agree. When Plan 8 adds analytics, this page changes in the same commit — the
 * tests fail until it does.
 */
const UPDATED = '2026-08-12';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — LiTex Textile & Technology"
  description="What this website collects, which is almost nothing: no cookies, no analytics, one disclosed third-party host. What happens to an enquiry, and for how long."
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    This site collects nothing about you that you did not choose to send it. That is not a policy
    position so much as a description of how it is built — no cookie of its own, no analytics
    script, and exactly one host other than this domain contacted anywhere on it: the anti-spam
    check on the enquiry form.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>

  <ContactBlock />

  <h2>What this website does</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No cookies.</strong> Nothing this site serves sets a cookie or writes to local
      storage. The one script it does not serve itself is the Turnstile widget described below,
      which is Cloudflare's code and behaves on Cloudflare's terms rather than ours.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No analytics.</strong> There is no analytics script, no tag manager and no pixel.
      Nobody is counting your visit.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>One third-party host.</strong> Fonts, images and stylesheets are served from this
      domain on every page, and so is every script but one: a page carrying an enquiry form also
      loads Cloudflare's Turnstile widget from challenges.cloudflare.com. Loading any other page
      contacts no host but this one.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>One kind of form.</strong> The enquiry form is the only thing on this site to submit,
      and using it is optional — contact by email or telephone works just as well, using the
      details above. What the form collects, and how long it is kept, is set out below.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>

  <p>
    The site is served by Cloudflare Pages. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes the technical
    information a browser sends in order to deliver a page — your IP address, the page requested,
    and your user agent — and retains it briefly for security and operational purposes. LiTex does
    not receive that data as a report and does not combine it with anything else.
  </p>

  <h2>If you send us an enquiry through this site</h2>

  <p>
    A form asks for your name, your company, an email address we can reply to and, if you choose
    to give it, your country. The rest is the enquiry itself — what you need, and, where a form
    asks for it, the product, grade, quantity and intended application. That is the whole of it:
    nothing is recorded that you did not type.
  </p>

  <p>
    Two of the fields are hidden. One records which form you submitted, so that a single endpoint
    can serve every form. The other is an empty box no visitor ever sees and only an automated
    script fills in; a submission that arrives with it filled is discarded and never stored.
    Neither field says anything about you.
  </p>

  <p>
    Your submission is written to Cloudflare Workers KV — the key-value store behind this site's
    form endpoint — and emailed to LiTex. The stored copy expires automatically after{' '}
    <strong>180 days</strong>. That expiry is set on the record at the moment it is written, so
    deletion is a
    property of the storage rather than something someone has to remember to do. The email that
    reaches the sales mailbox is then held on the terms in the next section.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>No IP address is recorded.</strong> The form endpoint does not read the address your
    submission came from, does not store it and does not pass it on — not even to Cloudflare
    Turnstile, whose verification API accepts an optional visitor IP that this site deliberately
    declines to send. What is kept is the contents of the form and the time it arrived. Cloudflare's
    own hosting logs, described above, are a separate matter and outside LiTex's hands.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Cloudflare Turnstile.</strong> A page carrying a form also loads a small script from
    challenges.cloudflare.com, and the endpoint checks its result before accepting anything. It
    establishes that a submission is coming from a person rather than from a script, which is what
    lets the form stay open to anyone at all without the sales mailbox filling with spam. It runs
    on the form pages only; no other page of this site requests it.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Resend.</strong> The enquiry email is delivered by Resend, engaged solely to carry it
    to LiTex. Your browser never contacts Resend — the request is made server-side, after your
    submission has already been stored.
  </p>

  <h2>If you email or telephone us</h2>

  <p>
    Then we hold whatever you send us: your name, your address, and what you asked about. We use it
    to answer you and to handle any resulting quotation, sample or order, and we keep it for as
    long as that business relationship needs. We do not sell it and we do not pass it to anyone
    outside the company for marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>

  <p>
    If you are in the EU or the UK, you can ask us for a copy of what we hold about you, ask us to
    correct it, or ask us to delete it. Write to{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> and say which. If a request is about an
    inquiry you sent us, telling us roughly when you sent it makes it much faster to find.
  </p>

  <h2>Mobile information</h2>

  {/* This paragraph deliberately ends without a full stop — so did
      archive/pages/privacy-policy.html, and the source note below claims it is carried
      over verbatim. Do not "fix" the punctuation; that would falsify the source note. */}
  <p class="quoted">
    No mobile information will be shared with third parties/affiliates for marketing/promotional
    purposes. All other categories exclude text messaging originator opt-in data and consent; this
    information will not be shared with any third parties
  </p>

  <p class="note" data-source-note>
    <small>
      Last updated {UPDATED}. The mobile-information paragraph is carried over verbatim from the
      previous LiTex privacy policy, where it was the entire text of the page.
    </small>
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lede { font-size: var(--t-20); color: var(--c-text-2); max-width: 58ch; }
  p, li { max-width: 70ch; }
  ul { padding-left: var(--s-6); }
  li { margin-bottom: var(--s-3); }
  .quoted {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--c-line);
    padding-left: var(--s-6);
    color: var(--c-text-2);
  }
  .note { color: var(--c-text-2); margin-top: var(--s-16); }
</style>
